---
import { siteUrl } from '../../utils/site';
import Concept from '../../layouts/Concept.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../components/Mermaid.astro';

const chart = `flowchart LR
  JSON["data/stage_configs/city-boundaries/&lt;area&gt;.json"] --> Builder["CityBoundaryBuilder"]
  Builder -->|"buildFloor: true"| Floor["Walkable Floor ConcavePolygonShape3D (layer 1)"]
  Builder --> Walls["Extruded Perimeter &amp; Cutout Walls (layer 1)"]
  Builder --> Respawn["player.fall_respawn_y"]
  Tool["#/floor-collider-builder"] <-->|"GET / POST dev API"| JSON
`;
---

<Concept title="City Walkable Boundaries">
  <div class="diagram"><Mermaid chart={chart} /></div>

  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>, <strong>SHALL</strong>, <strong>SHOULD</strong>, <strong>MAY</strong>, and <strong>OPTIONAL</strong> below are used as described in RFC 2119.</p>

  <p>Every Dairon City scene (<a href={siteUrl('/journey/city/market')}>Market</a>, <a href={siteUrl('/journey/city/underground')}>Underground</a>, <a href={siteUrl('/journey/city/office')}>Principal's Office</a>, and <a href={siteUrl('/journey/city/counter')}>Guild Counter</a>) <strong>MUST</strong> confine the player avatar to the intended walkable floor and <strong>MUST NOT</strong> rely on oversized rectangular <code>BoxShape3D</code> slabs or downward floor-probe raycasts alone.</p>

  <h2>Why floor raycasts alone are insufficient</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>Player._can_move_to</code> casts three downward rays ahead of normal walking and dodging, <strong>NOT</strong> during combo lunges, diagonal capsule slides along angled walls, or step-ups (<code>STEP_UP_MAX_HEIGHT = 0.5</code>).</li>
    <li>Visual stage floors extend beneath market stalls, raised planters, canal grates, apse bookcases, and dead-end exit corridors where no visual mesh collision exists.</li>
    <li>Therefore, each city area <strong>MUST</strong> combine accurate floor support with vertical blocking collision walls extruded on physics layer <code>1</code> (Environment).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Boundary sidecar schema</h2>
  <p>Walkable boundaries are authored as in-repo JSON sidecars at <code>data/stage_configs/city-boundaries/&lt;areaId&gt;.json</code> so boundary adjustments ship directly with the repository without rebuilding or republishing the external asset pack.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>version</code> (integer, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): schema version (<code>1</code>).</li>
    <li><code>areaId</code> (string, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): canonical city key — one of <code>"market"</code>, <code>"underground"</code>, <code>"office"</code>, or <code>"counter"</code>.</li>
    <li><code>stageId</code> (string, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): stage asset identifier (<code>"s00e_sa1"</code>, <code>"s00e_sa4"</code>, <code>"s00e_office"</code>, <code>"s00e_sa2"</code>).</li>
    <li><code>buildFloor</code> (boolean, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): when <code>true</code>, <code>CityBoundaryBuilder</code> triangulates <code>perimeter</code> minus floor-level <code>cutouts</code> into a walkable <code>ConcavePolygonShape3D</code> at <code>floorY</code>. When <code>false</code> (e.g. Guild Counter, whose sloped ramp uses <code>s00e_sa2-floor.glb</code>), only vertical walls and cutouts are built.</li>
    <li><code>floorY</code> (number, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): world-space Y elevation of the flat walkable floor and default base elevation of perimeter walls.</li>
    <li><code>wallBottomY</code> (number, <strong>OPTIONAL</strong>): overrides the base Y of extruded perimeter walls when an area spans multiple elevations (such as Guild Counter's <code>-10.67</code> hall and <code>-5.33</code> teleporter plaza).</li>
    <li><code>wallHeight</code> (number, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): vertical height (meters, <strong>MUST</strong> be &ge; <code>2.5</code>) extruded upward from the wall base so neither normal walking nor step-up / lunge motion can crest the barrier.</li>
    <li><code>fallRespawnY</code> (number, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): safety-net Y threshold applied to <code>player.fall_respawn_y</code>; if any physics defect drops the player below this height, the player <strong>MUST</strong> respawn at the area's spawn transform.</li>
    <li><code>perimeter</code> (array of <code>[x, z]</code> pairs, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>): closed, simple (non-self-intersecting) 2D polygon of at least 3 vertices in Godot world XZ coordinates defining the outer walkable boundary.</li>
    <li><code>cutouts</code> (array of objects, <strong>OPTIONAL</strong>): inner obstacle loops (stalls, crates, lamp posts, desks, counters). Each cutout defines <code>id</code>, <code>points</code> (3+ <code>[x, z]</code> pairs), optional <code>subtractFloor</code> (default <code>true</code> when at floor elevation), optional <code>wallBottomY</code>, and optional <code>wallHeight</code>.</li>
    <li><code>openings</code> (array of objects, <strong>OPTIONAL</strong>): metadata and optional wall-gap intervals (<code>edge</code> index, <code>tStart</code>, <code>tEnd</code> in <code>[0, 1]</code>, <code>wallBottomY</code>, or visual-only portal tags) marking gates, stairs, and doorways.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Runtime collision rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>CityBoundaryBuilder</code> <strong>MUST</strong> attach a <code>StaticBody3D</code> named <code>CityBoundary</code> with <code>collision_layer = 1</code> and <code>collision_mask = 0</code>.</li>
    <li>Extruded wall segments <strong>MUST</strong> emit double-sided vertical triangle faces so capsule collision queries resolve cleanly regardless of polygon winding order.</li>
    <li>Every area's default spawn, named spawn variants, NPC interaction stand-points, and area/interactive exit triggers <strong>MUST</strong> lie inside the walkable region with at least <code>0.45 m</code> clearance from blocking walls where the player stands.</li>
    <li>Exit corridors (Market's north Counter gate, Underground's north stairs, Office's <code>+Z</code> door, and Counter's south Market gate and east Office corridor) <strong>MUST</strong> enclose the trigger volume inside the perimeter pocket and place a blocking backstop wall immediately behind the trigger so wall-hugging players cannot bypass the transition into dead corridors or empty void.</li>
    <li>Shop and service NPCs standing behind physical counters or alcoves (such as Underground's Synthesis and Photon Collector counters) <strong>MUST</strong> expose an interaction volume wide enough to overlap the walkable side of the boundary wall.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Per-area requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Market (<code>market.json</code>)</strong>: <code>buildFloor: true</code> at <code>y = 0.0</code>. <strong>MUST</strong> trace the upper shop plaza (Weapon, Item, and Grind/Tekker fronts plus north Counter gate), narrow through the central avenue between the raised planters, and open into the lower arrival plaza and western Underground stairwell while cutting out solid plaza props. The visual shadow-catcher plane in <code>CityAreaBase._apply_ds_bake_look</code> <strong>MUST</strong> remain uncollided on its render layer.</li>
    <li><strong>Underground (<code>underground.json</code>)</strong>: <code>buildFloor: true</code> at <code>y = 0.0</code>. <strong>MUST</strong> trace the west and east octagonal platforms, central bridge, and north exit stairs while blocking the south sewer canal edge, rubble corners, shop counter recesses, and east vending machine.</li>
    <li><strong>Principal's Office (<code>office.json</code>)</strong>: <code>buildFloor: true</code> at <code>y = 0.0</code> with <code>wallHeight &ge; 4.5</code> so the curved apse perimeter confines both the <code>y = 0.0</code> lower hall and the <code>y = 1.05</code> upper library landing inside the bookcases and ladders, narrows to the <code>+Z</code> doorway trigger, and places an elevated cutout around the Principal's desk without obstructing <code>(0, 1.05, -3.9)</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Guild Counter (<code>counter.json</code>)</strong>: <code>buildFloor: false</code> (retaining <code>s00e_sa2-floor.glb</code> for the sloped <code>kaidan</code> stairs) with full-span perimeter walls, a cutout around the curved guild desk, and widened/backstopped exit pockets at the Market and Office transitions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Web authoring workflow</h2>
  <p>The <code>#/floor-collider-builder</code> web tool <strong>MUST</strong> provide a <strong>Boundary + Walls</strong> mode that loads any of the four city presets (including a procedural 3D preview of <code>OfficeLibraryRoom</code>), renders spawn/NPC/trigger reference pins and translucent extruded 3D walls, supports interactive vertex dragging, edge splitting, and obstacle cutouts, and writes updated JSON directly to <code>data/stage_configs/city-boundaries/&lt;areaId&gt;.json</code> via the local Vite dev server (with Copy/Download JSON fallbacks).</p>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/city/city_boundary_builder.gd</code> (<code>CityBoundaryBuilder</code>) — JSON loader, polygon clipping/triangulation, floor mesh builder, and double-sided vertical wall extruder.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/city/city_area_base.gd</code> (<code>CityAreaBase._apply_city_boundary</code>) — shared scene hook wiring collision construction and <code>player.fall_respawn_y</code>.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/city/city_market_controller.gd</code>, <code>city_underground_controller.gd</code>, <code>city_office_controller.gd</code>, <code>city_counter_controller.gd</code> — per-area boundary activation and trigger/NPC sizing.</li>
    <li><code>web/src/floor-collider-builder/FloorColliderBuilder.tsx</code> &amp; <code>web/vite-plugin-collider-export.ts</code> — visual polygon/cutout/wall authoring and dev-mode repository save endpoint.</li>
  </ul>
</Concept>
